        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What type of special quadrilateral is PQRS? Justify your answer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Rhombus, because all four sides are equal.",
          "worked": "The magnitudes of the four side vectors are equal, so all four sides of PQRS have equal length. Therefore PQRS is a rhombus.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q6-b-part",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What can be said about the directions of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ and $\\overrightarrow{RS}$? Justify your answer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Opposite directions; PQ and RS are opposite, parallel sides of a rhombus.",
          "worked": "Opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel. The arrows from P to Q and from R to S run in opposite senses along these parallel sides, so $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ and $\\overrightarrow{RS}$ have opposite directions.",
